Z||000002||Cheever2||11-19-2000||08:55 AM||||It's more like I don't know where to start.  I can select wallpaper from the usual Properties thing, but that's all I know to do.  I have no digital pictures of my own, so I'd like to use some off the Net.  <P>Maybe I should take a class instead of bothering anybody here, if it requires a long explanation (for me it probably would).<BR>My computer experience is with the big systems, not the pc-based home stuff.  Different world.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||overlord||11-19-2000||09:16 AM||||easy...just find a nice big  picture...probably at least 1024*768 in size...right click on it and "set as wallpaper"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Julian||11-19-2000||10:45 AM||||Cheve... you using Windows98 or 95?<BR>(8 has a feature that allows you to stretch a picture to fit your screen.<P>...and NO you are not bugging anyone... after all if we can post 189 notes on an airfreshner and a bazillion on sub-woofers why can't we answer a walpaper question? By the way ...got any single sisters? LOL<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/meralogo.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||11-19-2000||02:05 PM||||Cheever, if you're using Windows (95,98, or2K), then simply do this:<P>1.) Find a pic of a Fiero that you want to use.<P>2.) Right click it, then click on "save picture as".<P>3.)Then right click again and click on "save as wallpaper".<P>If you want, you can click on "my computer" on your desktop, then click on "control panel", then click on "display". Usually the first thing is wallpaper. On that screen you'll see a box that says "stretch, tile, or center"..pick the one you like best.<P>Thats it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||11-19-2000||02:09 PM||||95 has "stretch" only if Plus! is installed. Note, stretch will also shrink an image if it is too big.<P>You can use any picture you want but you need the crop it to 640x480, 800x600, or 1024x768 pixels. If you don't it will do some pretty od things when you stretch it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||11-19-2000||05:47 PM||||I haven't got any Fiero wallpaper (yet) but I do have a few 3D rendered landscape wallpapers available on my website if anyone's interested..<P> <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/backgrounds/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/backgrounds/index.html</A> <P>There are lots more coming soon, I just need to create the gallery index file and upload them.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000008||Cheever2||11-19-2000||09:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>...you can click on "my computer" on your desktop, then click on "control panel", then click on "display". Usually the first thing is wallpaper. On that screen you'll see a box that says "stretch, tile, or center"...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> I'm experimenting with the pic in the "86 SE DRAWING" topic, cause there's a pretty one of the car being raffled (looks like MY car).  I got it saved as wallpaper, although it doesn't take up the whole screen, just centered.  So I went into Start-Settings-Control Panel-Display, and it's there as "ACD WALLPAPER" (whatever ACD is), and I see the Center/Tile selection but nothing regarding the size.<BR>Almost forgot, I'm using Windows98.<BR>The size isn't bad, but the color of the wallpaper around it clashes horribly.<P><BR>||||reg||1
